From e1518485c8c8be4dd190493a1bdd99cccea0d606 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sukrit Jaidee <45908411+SukritJaAIproject@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:05:06 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(desktop): per-edition icons and browser-tab title in
 source (1.2.2)

The two desktop editions shared one icon and one page title, so they were
told apart only by file names; a post-build patcher made them distinct on
one machine but every rebuild reverted it. Now it is part of the build:

- desktop/icons/<edition>/{icon.ico,icon.png,favicon.png}, generated by
  desktop/icons/make_edition_icons.py (blue = current line, amber with a
  footer band = Snapshot 2026-09-12, green with an inset frame = the
  upcoming ISO 15118 edition).
- IMPS_ICON_DIR selects the artwork: icon.ico becomes win.icon, which
  electron-builder applies to the exe before signing and NSIS reuses for
  the installers, uninstaller, Apps & Features and shortcuts; icon.png is
  the BrowserWindow (taskbar/alt-tab) icon.
- desktop/scripts/stage-edition-resources.ps1 (replaces the snapshot-only
  stager) stages every edition: dashboard + sidecar from the build, the
  edition's summary, models and favicon. electron-builder copies extra
  resources concurrently, so the favicon inside the shared Next app cannot
  be overridden by a second resource entry.
- The browser-tab title follows the running edition from /health
  (edition-identity.ts, e.g. "iMPS Snapshot 2026-09-12 v1.1.2 - Fault
  Detection"), set after hydration so React does not revert it; the web
  deployment keeps "iMPS". Favicon link type fixed to image/png.
- Version 1.2.2 (snapshot edition 1.1.2 via IMPS_APP_VERSION).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
